# UI pull request screenshots

When a change affects anything a user can see (layout, styling, copy, a new screen, a dialog, empty/error states, or a user flow), the pull request must include screenshots of the updated UI.

Do this every time. Do not wait to be asked.

## What to attach

- The changed screen in its primary state
- Any new dialog, empty, error, or loading state the change introduces
- Enough of the surrounding page that a reviewer can tell what changed

Capture from the running app (browser), not a mock. Prefer PNG. Put files in `docs/screenshots/<short-change-name>/` on the PR branch and embed them in the PR description:

```md
## Screenshots

![Home form](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/<owner>/<repo>/<branch>/docs/screenshots/<name>/home.png)
```

On GitHub, use that raw.githubusercontent.com URL (or upload the images in the PR body) so they render before merge.

## Local helpers (development only)

`http://localhost:3456/?shot=progress`, `?shot=bypass`, and `?shot=fetch-error` open the review-progress dialog states so you can screenshot them without a live Vercel PR.
